# FieldSense frontend UI

Follow `docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md` (theme “Wellhead”, checklist, voice dictionary).

## Non-negotiables

- Tokens only: pine / copper / moss / stone / paper from CSS + Tailwind — no purple SaaS glow, no cream+terracotta poster look, no Inter/Roboto brand face.
- Brand “FieldSense” stays the strongest chrome signal; Fraunces display + Figtree body.
- Coverage refusals: summary + “We don’t have this data” — never an empty Results table (`rows` empty/null + `coverage.status === unsupported`).
- Chrome copy is operator-friendly (Who’s asking, Answer as of, See sources, New conversation). Keep API jargon out of labels.
- Question catalog: HOST tab = official test-data Q1–Q11 (copper); OURS = FieldSense showcase (moss). Keep them visually distinct.
- Cards only for interactive answer surfaces; empty state = title + one sentence + suggestion grid.
- Motion: message enter, suggestion hover, loading pulse — purposeful, not noisy.

## When editing UI

1. Extend `--fs-*` tokens rather than hard-coding hex in JSX.
2. Add human `COL_LABELS` for any new table fields.
3. If you change a pattern, update `docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md`.
